Title: The Glass of Water
Order: 22
Production Code: 1x22

INT. LIVINGSTON HALL - AUBREY'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

AMB: a clock striking two, otherwise silence

[[Aubrey Livingston]] wakes from the deepest sleep of his life to find he cannot move — held down by no visible hand, his eyes fixed open by no visible force.

The door to [[Dianthe Lusk]]'s room opens. She crosses to his bedside, listens to his breathing, and swaps the glass of water on his table for one she's carried in hidden.

She turns to go. A hand closes on her shoulder — his.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(low, terrible)
Drink.

DIANTHE LUSK
(horrified)
Aubrey — mercy, let me explain—

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Drain the glass to Reuel.

DIANTHE LUSK
(taking it)
To Reuel.

She empties it. He walks her back to her door and, with mocking gentleness, kisses her hand goodnight.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Farewell, my love. When we meet, 'twill be —

DIANTHE LUSK
In judgment, Aubrey. May God have mercy on both our guilty souls.
